    {
        "content": "<p>Following up on this: with the benefit of having <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"479299\">@Jovan Gerbscheid</span> in person to patiently answer my questions, it seems the right way to do this is similar to <code>to_additive</code> and <code>to_dual</code> that make use of the machinery provided by <code>Mathlib.Tactic.Translate</code>. </p>\n<p>I think we would define a new attribute, perhaps named <code>to_swap</code>, whose scope is flipping a given relation for certain predicates. I think this really should live in Mathlib eventually (it applies for instance to pairs like <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Relator.LeftUnique#doc\">docs#Relator.LeftUnique</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Relator.RightUnique#doc\">docs#Relator.RightUnique</a>), but let's try it out here in CSLib first. Not particularly urgent, but I think it could be a nice feature.</p>",
        "id": 594911734,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1778692507
    }
]